body:
Amount rendering bypasses the column’s `cell` renderer and always uses `formatCurrency(value)` with the default currency. If a schema column is explicitly `type: 'currency'` (or has a custom `cell`), this will ignore currency metadata/precision and can render inconsistently vs the grid/table view. Prefer `amountCol.cell` when present (falling back to `formatCurrency` only when there is no renderer).
```suggestion
                        {(() => {
                          const amountValue = row[amountCol.accessorKey];
                          if (amountCol.cell) {
                            return amountCol.cell(amountValue, row);
                          }
                          if (typeof amountValue === 'number') {
                            return formatCurrency(amountValue);
                          }
                          return amountValue ?? '—';
                        })()}
```
